<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on low volumes.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on low volumes.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday with arrivals at around 5,000 tonnes, dealers said. Volumes were low.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were at previous level in very thin trade.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady in very limited trading. Rapeseed extraction prices were down by 100 rupees per tonne in FOR and prices were down by $2-$3 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $270 to $271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $130 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,400 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4375 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
